IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `qld-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 8 -- Terms and references in Acts, first group (ss 32 to 32F).
-- This group is about defined terms, words and their forms, "may" and "must", persons, de facto partners, computer records and commencement.

§ `Part 8 -- Terms and references in Acts (ss 32 to 32F)`

§§ `ss 32 to 32AB -- defined terms`

-- src:574 | If an Act defines a word or expression, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the word or expression have corresponding meanings.
@ref s 32 (src:574-574)
GIVEN `an Act defines a word or expression` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is another part of speech or grammatical form of the word or expression` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the other part of speech or grammatical form has a corresponding meaning (s 32)` IS
    IF `an Act defines a word or expression` AND `it is another part of speech or grammatical form of the word or expression` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 32A: "except so far as the context or subject matter otherwise indicates or requires".
-- FORK once the context or subject matter otherwise indicates or requires: NOTHING (the definition's application is then not settled by s 32A) || JUST FALSE
-- src:576 | Definitions in or applicable to an Act apply except so far as the context or subject matter otherwise indicates or requires.
@ref s 32A (src:576-576)
GIVEN `the definition is in or applicable to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context or subject matter otherwise indicates or requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the definition applies (s 32A)` IS
    IF NOT `the definition is in or applicable to the Act`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the context or subject matter otherwise indicates or requires` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:578 | A definition in or applying to an Act applies to the entire Act.
@ref s 32AA (src:578-578)
GIVEN `it is a definition in or applying to an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the definition applies to the provision (s 32AA)` IS
    IF `it is a definition in or applying to an Act` AND `the provision is in the Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 32AB: a word defined non-exhaustively for another Act and also defined in this Act.
-- src:580 | If—
-- src:581 | (a) a word or expression is defined non-exhaustively for the purposes of an Act other than this Act (the non-exhaustive definition); and
-- src:582 | (b) the word or expression is also defined in this Act (the Interpretation Act definition);
-- src:583 | then, for the purposes of the first Act—
-- src:584 | (c) the non-exhaustive definition does not exclude or limit, but may extend, the meaning of the word or expression given by the Interpretation Act definition; and
@ref s 32AB (src:580-584)
GIVEN `a word or expression is defined non-exhaustively for the purposes of an Act other than this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word or expression is also defined in this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the non-exhaustive definition excludes or limits the meaning given by the Interpretation Act definition (s 32AB(c))` IS
    IF `a word or expression is defined non-exhaustively for the purposes of an Act other than this Act` AND `the word or expression is also defined in this Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:580 | If—
-- src:581 | (a) a word or expression is defined non-exhaustively for the purposes of an Act other than this Act (the non-exhaustive definition); and
-- src:582 | (b) the word or expression is also defined in this Act (the Interpretation Act definition);
-- src:583 | then, for the purposes of the first Act—
-- src:584 | (c) the non-exhaustive definition does not exclude or limit, but may extend, the meaning of the word or expression given by the Interpretation Act definition; and
@ref s 32AB (src:580-584)
GIVEN `a word or expression is defined non-exhaustively for the purposes of an Act other than this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word or expression is also defined in this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the non-exhaustive definition may extend the meaning given by the Interpretation Act definition (s 32AB(c))` IS
    IF `a word or expression is defined non-exhaustively for the purposes of an Act other than this Act` AND `the word or expression is also defined in this Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:585 | (d) the non-exhaustive and Interpretation Act definitions are to be read in the context of each other and the other provisions of the first Act, but, if the definitions so read are inconsistent, the Interpretation Act definition is displaced.
@ref s 32AB (src:585-585)
GIVEN `a word or expression is defined non-exhaustively for the purposes of an Act other than this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word or expression is also defined in this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the definitions, read in the context of each other and the other provisions of the first Act, are inconsistent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Interpretation Act definition is displaced (s 32AB(d))` IS
    IF `a word or expression is defined non-exhaustively for the purposes of an Act other than this Act` AND `the word or expression is also defined in this Act` AND `the definitions, read in the context of each other and the other provisions of the first Act, are inconsistent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 32B and 32C -- gender, number`

-- src:587 | In an Act, words indicating a gender include each other gender.
@ref s 32B (src:587-587)
GIVEN `the word indicates a gender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the word includes each other gender (s 32B)` IS
    IF `the word indicates a gender` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Grammatical number of a word` IS ONE OF
    singular
    plural

-- src:589 | In an Act—
-- src:590 | (a) words in the singular include the plural; and
-- src:591 | (b) words in the plural include the singular.
@ref s 32C (src:589-591)
GIVEN `the number of the word` IS A `Grammatical number of a word`
      `the number asked about` IS A `Grammatical number of a word`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the word includes the number asked about (s 32C)` IS
    CONSIDER `the number of the word`
    WHEN singular THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN plural THEN JUST TRUE

§§ `s 32CA -- Meaning of may and must etc.`

DECLARE `Word used in relation to a power` IS ONE OF
    `the word may, or a similar word or expression`
    `the word must, or a similar word or expression`
    `another word`

DECLARE `What a word used in relation to a power indicates` IS ONE OF
    `that the power may be exercised or not exercised, at discretion`
    `that the power is required to be exercised`

-- src:593 | (1) In an Act, the word may, or a similar word or expression, used in relation to a power indicates that the power may be exercised or not exercised, at discretion.
@ref s 32CA(1) (src:593-593)
-- src:594 | (2) In an Act, the word must, or a similar word or expression, used in relation to a power indicates that the power is required to be exercised.
@ref s 32CA(2) (src:594-594)
GIVEN word IS A `Word used in relation to a power`
GIVETH A MAYBE `What a word used in relation to a power indicates`
DECIDE `what the word indicates about the power (s 32CA(1) and (2))` IS
    CONSIDER word
    WHEN `the word may, or a similar word or expression` THEN JUST `that the power may be exercised or not exercised, at discretion`
    WHEN `the word must, or a similar word or expression` THEN JUST `that the power is required to be exercised`
    WHEN `another word` THEN NOTHING

-- src:595 | (3) To remove any doubt, it is declared that this section applies to an Act passed after 1 January 1992 despite any presumption or rule of interpretation.
@ref s 32CA(3) (src:595-595)
GIVEN `the date the Act was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32CA applies to the Act despite any presumption or rule of interpretation (s 32CA(3))` IS
    IF `the date the Act was passed` GREATER THAN Date 1 1 1992 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 32CB -- Words and expressions used in amending Acts`

-- src:597 | (1) Words and expressions used in an Act that amends another law have the same meanings as they have in the other law.
@ref s 32CB(1) (src:597-597)
GIVEN `the Act amends another law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `words and expressions used in the Act have the same meanings as they have in the other law (s 32CB(1))` IS
    IF `the Act amends another law` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:598 | (2) Subsection (1) does not limit section 22 (Act and amending Acts to be read as one).
@ref s 32CB(2) (src:598-598)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32CB(1) limits s 22 (s 32CB(2))` IS FALSE

§§ `s 32D -- References to persons generally`

DECLARE `Kind of entity` IS ONE OF
    `a corporation`
    `an individual`
    `anything else`

-- src:601 | (1) In an Act, a reference to a person generally includes a reference to a corporation as well as an individual.
@ref s 32D(1) (src:601-601)
GIVEN `the reference is to a person generally` IS A BOOLEAN
      entity IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to a person generally includes a reference to the entity (s 32D(1))` IS
    IF NOT `the reference is to a person generally`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER entity
        WHEN `anything else` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:602 | (2) Subsection (1) is not displaced merely because there is an express reference to either an individual or a corporation elsewhere in the Act.
@ref s 32D(2) (src:602-602)
GIVEN `there is an express reference to either an individual or a corporation elsewhere in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection (1) is displaced merely because of an express reference to either an individual or a corporation elsewhere in the Act (s 32D(2))` IS
    IF `there is an express reference to either an individual or a corporation elsewhere in the Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of reference to a person` IS ONE OF
    `a reference to a person generally`
    `an express reference to a corporation`
    `an express reference to an individual`

`the words given as examples of references to a person generally` MEANS
    LIST "another", "anyone", "no-one", "one", "party", "person", "someone", "whoever"

`the words given as examples of express references to a corporation` MEANS
    LIST "body corporate", "company", "corporation sole"

`the words given as examples of express references to an individual` MEANS
    LIST "adult", "child", "spouse"

-- The three example lists are examples ("Examples of ..."), so a word that is on none of them is not answered: NOTHING.
-- src:603 | Examples of references to a person generally—
-- src:604 | another
-- src:605 | anyone
-- src:606 | no-one
-- src:607 | one
-- src:608 | party
-- src:609 | person
-- src:610 | someone
-- src:611 | whoever
@ref s 32D, examples of references to a person generally (src:603-611)
-- src:612 | Examples of express references to a corporation—
-- src:613 | body corporate
-- src:614 | company
-- src:615 | corporation sole
@ref s 32D, examples of express references to a corporation (src:612-615)
-- src:616 | Examples of express references to an individual—
-- src:617 | adult
-- src:618 | child
-- src:619 | spouse
@ref s 32D, examples of express references to an individual (src:616-619)
GIVEN word IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of reference to a person`
DECIDE `the kind of reference the word is given as an example of (s 32D)` IS
    IF elem word `the words given as examples of references to a person generally`
    THEN JUST `a reference to a person generally`
    ELSE IF elem word `the words given as examples of express references to a corporation`
         THEN JUST `an express reference to a corporation`
         ELSE IF elem word `the words given as examples of express references to an individual`
              THEN JUST `an express reference to an individual`
              ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 32DA -- Meaning of de facto partner`

-- (1): "a reference to a de facto partner is a reference to either 1 of 2 persons who are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis but who are not married to each other or related by family."
-- src:621 | (1) In an Act, a reference to a de facto partner is a reference to either 1 of 2 persons who are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis but who are not married to each other or related by family.
@ref s 32DA(1) (src:621-621)
GIVEN `the 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are married to each other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are related by family` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `each of the 2 persons is a de facto partner of the other (s 32DA(1))` IS
    JUST (`the 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` AND (NOT `they are married to each other`) AND (NOT `they are related by family`))

DECLARE `Circumstance of 2 persons` IS ONE OF
    `the nature and extent of their common residence`
    `the length of their relationship`
    `whether or not a sexual relationship exists or existed`
    `the degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and any arrangement for financial support`
    `their ownership, use and acquisition of property`
    `the degree of mutual commitment to a shared life, including the care and support of each other`
    `the care and support of children`
    `the performance of household tasks`
    `the reputation and public aspects of their relationship`
    `any other circumstance`

-- (2): "any of their circumstances may be taken into account, including, for example" the nine listed: every circumstance may be taken into account.
-- src:622 | (2) In deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis, any of their circumstances may be taken into account, including, for example, any of the following circumstances—
-- src:623 | (a) the nature and extent of their common residence;
-- src:624 | (b) the length of their relationship;
-- src:625 | (c) whether or not a sexual relationship exists or existed;
-- src:626 | (d) the degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and any arrangement for financial support;
-- src:627 | (e) their ownership, use and acquisition of property;
-- src:628 | (f) the degree of mutual commitment to a shared life, including the care and support of each other;
-- src:629 | (g) the care and support of children;
-- src:630 | (h) the performance of household tasks;
-- src:631 | (i) the reputation and public aspects of their relationship.
@ref s 32DA(2) (src:622-631)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `Circumstance of 2 persons`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the circumstance may be taken into account in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(2))` IS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `any other circumstance` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:632 | (3) No particular finding in relation to any circumstance is to be regarded as necessary in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis.
@ref s 32DA(3) (src:632-632)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a particular finding in relation to any circumstance is necessary in deciding whether 2 persons are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(3))` IS FALSE

-- (4): not to be regarded as living together as a couple "only because they have a common residence".
-- src:633 | (4) Two persons are not to be regarded as living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis only because they have a common residence.
@ref s 32DA(4) (src:633-633)
GIVEN `the only ground is that they have a common residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2 persons are regarded as living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (s 32DA(4))` IS
    IF `the only ground is that they have a common residence` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:634 | (5) For subsection (1)—
-- src:635 | (a) the gender of the persons is not relevant; and
@ref s 32DA(5) (src:634-635)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gender of the persons is relevant for s 32DA(1) (s 32DA(5)(a))` IS FALSE

-- (5)(b): the Marriage Act 1961 (Cwlth), section 23B is not among the sources, so whether the persons would be within a prohibited relationship is an input.
-- src:636 | (b) a person is related by family to another person if the person and the other person would be within a prohibited relationship within the meaning of the Marriage Act 1961 (Cwlth), section 23B, if they were parties to a marriage to which that section applies.
@ref s 32DA(5) (src:636-636)
GIVEN `the person and the other person would be within a prohibited relationship within the meaning of the Marriage Act 1961 (Cwlth), section 23B, if they were parties to a marriage to which that section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is related by family to the other person (s 32DA(5)(b))` IS
    JUST `the person and the other person would be within a prohibited relationship within the meaning of the Marriage Act 1961 (Cwlth), section 23B, if they were parties to a marriage to which that section applies`

-- (6): "unless the Act expressly provides to the contrary" -- the commencement of s 32DA is not stated in the text, so whether the Act was enacted before it is an input.
-- FORK once the Act expressly provides to the contrary: NOTHING (this subsection no longer answers) || JUST FALSE
-- src:637 | (6) In an Act enacted before the commencement of this section, a reference to a spouse includes a reference to a de facto partner as defined in this section unless the Act expressly provides to the contrary.
@ref s 32DA(6) (src:637-637)
GIVEN `the Act was enacted before the commencement of s 32DA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act expressly provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to a spouse includes a reference to a de facto partner as defined in s 32DA (s 32DA(6))` IS
    IF `the Act was enacted before the commencement of s 32DA` AND (NOT `the Act expressly provides to the contrary`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 32E -- Production of records kept in computers etc.`

-- "unless the court, tribunal or person otherwise directs"
-- FORK once the court, tribunal or person otherwise directs: NOTHING (the requirement is then as directed and s 32E(c) and (d) do not answer) || JUST FALSE
-- src:639 | If a person who keeps a record of information by way of a mechanical, electronic or other device is required by or under an Act—
-- src:640 | (a) to produce the information or a document containing the information to a court, tribunal or person; or
-- src:641 | (b) to make a document containing the information available for inspection by a court, tribunal or person;
-- src:642 | then, unless the court, tribunal or person otherwise directs—
-- src:643 | (c) the requirement obliges the person to produce or make available for inspection, as the case may be, a document that reproduces the information in a form capable of being understood by the court, tribunal or person; and
@ref s 32E (src:639-643)
GIVEN `a person who keeps a record of information by way of a mechanical, electronic or other device is required by or under an Act to produce the information or a document containing it, or to make a document containing it available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court, tribunal or person otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requirement obliges the person to produce or make available a document reproducing the information in a form capable of being understood (s 32E(c))` IS
    IF `a person who keeps a record of information by way of a mechanical, electronic or other device is required by or under an Act to produce the information or a document containing it, or to make a document containing it available for inspection` AND (NOT `the court, tribunal or person otherwise directs`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:644 | (d) the production to the court, tribunal or person of the document in that form complies with the requirement.
@ref s 32E (src:644-644)
GIVEN `a person who keeps a record of information by way of a mechanical, electronic or other device is required by or under an Act to produce the information or a document containing it, or to make a document containing it available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court, tribunal or person otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the production of the document in that form complies with the requirement (s 32E(d))` IS
    IF `a person who keeps a record of information by way of a mechanical, electronic or other device is required by or under an Act to produce the information or a document containing it, or to make a document containing it available for inspection` AND (NOT `the court, tribunal or person otherwise directs`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 32F -- References to commencement`

-- (1): a reference to commencement for an Act or provision is a reference to the time the Act or provision comes into operation.
-- src:646 | (1) In an Act, a reference to commencement for an Act or a provision of an Act is a reference to the time the Act or provision comes into operation.
@ref s 32F(1) (src:646-646)
GIVEN `the time the Act or provision comes into operation` IS A `Moment in a day`
GIVETH A `Moment in a day`
DECIDE `the time a reference to commencement refers to (s 32F(1))` IS
    `the time the Act or provision comes into operation`

DECLARE `Commencement a reference to the commencement refers to` IS ONE OF
    `the commencement of the provision in which the reference occurs`
    `the commencement of the Act or provision indicated`

-- src:647 | (2) In a provision of an Act, a reference to the commencement without indicating a particular Act or provision is a reference to the commencement of the provision in which the reference occurs.
-- src:648 | Example of subsection (2)—
-- src:649 | If section 24(3) of an Act stated ‘This section expires 1 month after the commencement’, ‘the commencement’ referred to is the commencement of section 24(3).
@ref s 32F(2) (src:647-649)
GIVEN `the reference indicates a particular Act or provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Commencement a reference to the commencement refers to`
DECIDE `what a reference to the commencement refers to (s 32F(2))` IS
    IF `the reference indicates a particular Act or provision`
    THEN `the commencement of the Act or provision indicated`
    ELSE `the commencement of the provision in which the reference occurs`
